# Shared Spaces #

# Every slide in this deck is shared. Its text lives on the Internet #
# Computer canister, in the space named shared, not in your browser: #
# a slide anyone adds here, everyone who opens the deck sees. #

# To add one: the + (Add New Slide) in the slide controls. The name #
# it offers starts with Shared Spaces /, and that prefix is what puts #
# a slide here -- keep it, and the slide is shared. Rename it out of #
# the deck, and it is yours alone again. #

# How it works: Hazel stores each slide under a key, doc:<name>. A #
# key that starts doc:Shared Spaces / goes to the canister's shared #
# space, whatever space the rest of the page uses, and the deck's #
# slides are read from that space when the page loads. So reload to #
# see slides added since. #

# For the demo, anyone may write: add, edit, rename or delete. Two #
# people editing one slide at once is last write wins. A slide's #
# agent chat is not shared; it stays with whoever had it. #

# Opened outside the canister build, this deck is an ordinary one, #
# kept in your browser like any other. #

# This slide is shared too: edit it, and everyone sees the edit. #
()
